WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.252
Modern expertise is often distributed.

2
00:00:02.252 --> 00:00:11.712
A team may hold more capability than any one individual because knowledge is spread across people, documentation, tools, automation, and routines.

3
00:00:11.712 --> 00:00:14.865
Shared mental models help the group coordinate.

4
00:00:14.865 --> 00:00:18.920
Handoffs help expertise move across time and role boundaries.

5
00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:25.226
Documentation makes important reasoning visible instead of trapping it inside one person's memory.

6
00:00:25.226 --> 00:00:32.884
Tools can extend expertise when they reduce routine burden, preserve context, surface patterns, or make review easier.

7
00:00:32.884 --> 00:00:36.037
Automation can help with consistency and speed.

8
00:00:36.037 --> 00:00:40.992
AI assistance can summarize, draft, compare, search, classify, or generate options.

9
00:00:40.992 --> 00:00:44.146
But tool output still needs expert review.

10
00:00:44.146 --> 00:00:51.803
A tool can produce fluent results without understanding context, consequences, or the organization's tolerance for risk.

11
00:00:51.803 --> 00:00:54.506
A major challenge is avoiding deskilling.

12
00:00:54.506 --> 00:01:05.317
If people accept tool output without inspection, they may lose the habit of checking assumptions, noticing exceptions, and understanding why an answer is appropriate.

13
00:01:05.317 --> 00:01:09.372
Better designs keep humans engaged in the judgment loop.

14
00:01:09.372 --> 00:01:18.831
They use tools to make expertise more effective, not to hide the work so completely that no one can evaluate it.

15
00:01:18.831 --> 00:01:26.039
Teams can make expertise reusable by capturing examples, decision records, review notes, checklists, and lessons learned.

16
00:01:26.039 --> 00:01:32.796
They can teach expertise by explaining how strong performers think, not just what they conclude.

17
00:01:32.796 --> 00:01:36.400
AI-assisted work makes this even more important.

18
00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:46.310
The strongest teams use tools to amplify judgment, while preserving accountability, review, and the ability to explain why a decision makes sense.
